.TH TRUE 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
true \- do nothing, successfully
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B true
does nothing and exits with status 0. Any arguments are ignored.
.PP
.BR sh (1)
has
.B true
built in as well; this program is what runs when it's called by path or from
another program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
